Z||000008||Raydar||03-19-2001||09:19 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KnightRyder31:<BR><B>Man, its one hell of a job to change the freaken plugs on this car.<BR>You guys ever try changing plugs on a 3.1?<BR>You have to pry the engine forward!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Try parking the car pointed downhill. The weight of the car should rock the engine forward.<BR>Aren't the coil packs on top of the engine?<BR>You should be able to check for spark, there. <BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000009||rogergarrison||03-19-2001||11:44 AM||||did it make any different noises when you drove it last. Did it overheat. What the oil pressure reading before and now. how low was the oil before you added. does it just run crappy, or backfire, smoke. Did you do anything since it was running fine. like change spark plug wires, ignition module, etc.||||reg||1
Z||000010||87GT||03-19-2001||03:53 PM||||I sold my 94 Grand Prix SE 3.1 V6 to a friend of mine 2 years ago.  He drove it until about 3 weeks ago, when the timing belt slipped and destroyed his motor.  He was going down the road and the car just started losing power.  It starts up but sounds like **** .  It has bent the valves and damaged other various things.  It has 112K miles on it.  Your symptoms sound the same as what happened to his.  Hope this isnt the problem for your sake.||||reg||1
Z||000011||87GT||03-19-2001||04:03 PM||||I forgot to mention that my cousin who is a mechanic, just put back together a 3.4 in a Lumina that had the belt slip.  About $1400 to repair that car.  ||||reg||1
